    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1141">

                <pb facs="0818" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/64.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Miller.</hi><anchor
                        n="97" xml:id="d1141-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-15T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>State to local authorities that Department is informed that some American
                    citizens who have been forced by recent disturbed conditions to leave vicinity
                    of Tampico own leases on property that vicinity on which rentals are coming due
                    very soon which cannot be paid now because of conditions prevailing and that it
                    is expected that the authorities will perceive the justice of taking no action
                    in forfeiture of leases until owners have had reasonable time to pay rent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1141-f1" n="97" type="source" xml:id="d1141-f1-content">
                <p>Same to the American Consul at Durango except changing words “local authorities
                    “to “Carranza.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
